# CardModal — UI Overhaul

Reference images: `fixes_updates_references/` (Card_main_view.png, Card_main_view_added_items.png, Card_triple_dot_menu.png)
Mimic the reference images closely — they represent the target UX.

---

## Priority 1 — Removals (no dependencies)

- **Remove** the triple-dot (⋯) menu button and all associated menu items/logic entirely.

---

## Priority 2 — Top Bar Layout

Left side:
- Display the **List** the card currently belongs to as a **dropdown**.
- Selecting a different list moves the card to that list.

Right side (left to right):
- **Watch toggle** (Eye icon) — see behavior below.
- **Close button** (existing "X") — no changes needed.

---

## Priority 3 — Watch Toggle Behavior

- **Enabled state**: standard Eye icon.
- **Disabled state**: Eye icon with a slash through it.
- **Auto-enable**: when a user is added as a card member, Watch is automatically enabled for that user.
- **Auto-disable**: when a user is removed from a card, Watch is automatically disabled for that user.
- **Creating a card** does NOT automatically enable Watch.

---

## Priority 4 — Inline Title Editing

- The card title is editable directly in the modal.
- Click the title → enters edit mode.
- Confirm with **Enter/Return** or by clicking away → exits edit mode, changes persist.

---

## Priority 5 — Card Body Section Order

Default visible sections: **Description**, **Comments**.
All other sections appear only after being added. When present, render in this order (left-to-right, top-to-bottom):

1. Members
2. Labels
3. Due Date
4. Description
5. Attachments
6. Comments

> Checklist is NOT a feature at this time — do not implement or reference it.